    {
      "name": "Programmed to Serve",
      "type": "trait",
      "_id": "citActor34Item10",
      "img": "modules/impmal-core/assets/icons/blank.webp",
      "system": {
        "notes": {
          "player": "",
          "gm": "<p>Every Servitor has a pre-programed task to perform. They will continue to operate on their programmed functions until re-programmed with a Hard (−20) Tech (Augmetics) Test. The individual that programmed (or re-programmed) the Servitor can give it simple orders.  Prey for the Hunters: If the Harrier Skull moves at least within its own zone, any Grapple-Hawks or similar construucts within Long Range and line of sight must pass a Difficult (-10) Willpower test at the beginning of their next Turn. If they pass, they act normally. If they fail, they must directly move towards the Harrier-Skull and attempt to grapple it. A grapple-hawk that passes its willpower test may ignore the specific Harrier Skull in subsequent rounds, but may be affected by others. Grapple-Hawks ignore all other targets until it has caught the Harrier Skull. If the Grapple-Hawk has a controller, they may attempt to override the Grapple-Hawk's targeting with a Difficult (-10) Tech test during their turn.</p>"
        },
